\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1 O love divne, how sweet Thou art! 
\par When shall I find my willing heart 
\par All taken up by Thee?
\par I thirst, I faint, I die to prove 
\par The greatness of redeeming love, 
\par The love of Christ to me.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2 Stronger His love than death or hell;
\par Its riches are unsearchable;
\par The first-born sons of light 
\par Desire in vain itds depths to see,
\par They cannot reach the mystery,
\par The length, and breadth, and height.
\par 
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3 God only knows the love of God; 
\par O that it now were shed abroad 
\par In this poor stony heart!
\par For love I sigh, for love I pine:
\par This only portion, Lord, be mine,
\par Be mine this better part!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4 O that I could for ever sit 
\par Lke Mary at the Master's feet!
\par Be this my happy choice:
\par My only care, delight, annd bliss, 
\par My joy, my heacen on earth, be this-
\par To hear the Bridegroom's voice!
\par 
\par 
\par \f1 
